  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EMERGENCY FOOD SECURITY AND NUTRITION SUPPORT TO VULNERABLE REFUGEES AND HOST COMMUNITIES IN WHITE NILE STATE - SUDAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposed project will target 838 Households (HHs) including IDPs, refugees and host communities to be assisted with: Goat restocking (5 goats per HH, targeting 748 HHs), Fish processing training (wet salted fish, net making and dry fish) and start up kits, targeting 74 women and youth headed HHs from refugees and host community 50% each, and Fishing training and start up kits, targeting 16 youth Headed HHs, to be assisted in a safe, accessible, accountable, and inclusive manner; this intervention includes training on boat making, fishing and cold storage.</narrative>
  </description>
